  * ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  */
 
+/*
+ * Dan 2026-08-19: "the global header should stretch across the top of the page."
+ * It was rendering as a narrow pill floating in the middle of a black page.
+ *
+ * Nothing here was constraining it. The header is dropped into HomePage's
+ * .container, which is `display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items:
+ * center` — and a flex item that is not stretched shrink-wraps to its own
+ * content and gets centred. So the bar was exactly as wide as the icons inside
+ * it, bottom border and all.
+ *
+ * Three lines fix it and none of them depend on the parent behaving:
+ *   align-self: stretch  — overrides the parent's align-items: center, for this
+ *                          element only, so HomePage keeps centring everything
+ *                          else it centres.
+ *   width: 100%          — covers the parents that are not flex containers
+ *                          (AppLayout renders the same header in a block).
+ *   box-sizing           — keeps the 12px horizontal padding INSIDE the 100%,
+ *                          instead of pushing the bar 24px past the viewport
+ *                          and producing a sideways scrollbar.
+ */
 .header {
   background: #000000;
   padding: 8px 12px;
@@ -16,6 +36,9 @@
   z-index: 100;
   gap: 8px;
   flex-wrap: nowrap;
+  width: 100%;
+  align-self: stretch;
+  box-sizing: border-box;
 }
 
 .headerLeft {
